// exe globals of the .data blocks below that no recovered TU defines, initialized with the exe's values.
// One definition per exe address (tools/datacheck.py checks address, size and initializer); the other names
// users declare at an address are mapped to it with /alternatename. Class objects are byte images up to the
// next known exe global; their constructors (the owning TU's .text$di initializer) are not run by this unit,
// see the zero-blob list in work/sfr22/outside-summary.md. A recovered owner moves a definition to its TU.
// The hook DLL binds every name to the exe's own global (symbols table), so nothing here is compiled into it
// (docs/RECOVERY.md sec. 9).
// Group 143a51160 starts at 0x143a51180: its first 0x20 bytes are pcre's own globals (pcre_free 0x143a51160 ...),
// which the engine's pcre_globals.c defines.
// Groups 143a07430 / 143a284b0 start at 0x143a07838 / 0x143a288b8: their first 0x408 bytes are the efd::ClassInfo
// objects PropService::ms_ClassInfo / PropertyVisualizationService::ms_ClassInfo, which the engine's
// PropService.cpp / PropertyVisualizationService.cpp define; the names users declare there are mapped to them.
// 0x143a288b8-0x143a28a30 after it are GB message-handler statics as well (MessageHandlerImpl /
// MessageWrapperSubclassHandler objects of PropertyVisualizationService and VisualTrackerService, which
// VisualTrackerService::OnInit and the engine TUs' initializers use), so this unit starts at 0x143a28a30.
